Task 2: Validation and Error Handling

Validation Rules

To ensure data quality and avoid bad inputs, I added the following validations:

Name
Required
Minimum length: 2 characters
Email
Required
Must follow valid email format
User ID
Must exist when performing GET, PUT, DELETE
Error Handling

Proper error handling is critical for both developers and users of the API.

400 – Bad Request
{
  "error": "Invalid email format"
}
404 – Not Found
{
  "error": "User not found"
}
500 – Internal Server Error
{
  "error": "Something went wrong. Please try again later."
}
My Approach

I focused on keeping the API simple and predictable.

Used standard REST structure
Ensured each endpoint has a clear purpose
Included meaningful responses instead of generic ones

I also made sure validation and error handling are clear, since these are usually where integrations fail in real systems.

Business Relevance

This API can support:

Customer onboarding
Profile management
Integration with other systems (e.g., CRM, support tools)

From a business perspective:

Clean APIs reduce integration issues
Good validation improves data quality
Clear error messages reduce support tickets
